\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.7}What the unmatched play is}{12}{subsection.3.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:residual}{{3.7}{12}{What the unmatched play is}{subsection.3.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The residual is real, and it is not in the class.} (\textbf  {a}) Coverage as the hypothesis class is widened. The classes are nested, so the segments are disjoint and stack to one. The tick is where the same three classes reach on shuffled play, in which the focal agent's own action sequence is permuted in place while its cooperation rate and the opponent's realised sequence are held fixed; coverage to the left of the tick is what the fit buys by chance. (\textbf  {b}) How much history the next move uses. $\Delta $BIC of nested predictors of the next action against a memoryless model, scored on identical rows so the comparison is about history and not sample size. The ring marks each model's selected depth; all four select memory-two. (\textbf  {c}) Why even a fit rarely names a rule. Ten rounds seldom visit all four conditioning states, so rules differing only in an unvisited state are indistinguishable on that game. Bars pool all 4{,}800 agent-games.}}{13}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:residual}{{6}{13}{\textbf {The residual is real, and it is not in the class.} (\textbf {a}) Coverage as the hypothesis class is widened. The classes are nested, so the segments are disjoint and stack to one. The tick is where the same three classes reach on shuffled play, in which the focal agent's own action sequence is permuted in place while its cooperation rate and the opponent's realised sequence are held fixed; coverage to the left of the tick is what the fit buys by chance. (\textbf {b}) How much history the next move uses. $\Delta $BIC of nested predictors of the next action against a memoryless model, scored on identical rows so the comparison is about history and not sample size. The ring marks each model's selected depth; all four select memory-two. (\textbf {c}) Why even a fit rarely names a rule. Ten rounds seldom visit all four conditioning states, so rules differing only in an unvisited state are indistinguishable on that game. Bars pool all 4{,}800 agent-games}{figure.caption.13}{}}
